Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 19 CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma of right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 5 CM   WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  MARGINS NEGATIVE  SEE NOTE  2  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH PAGETOID SPREAD  THE INFILTRATING COMPONENT EXTENDS TO SURGICAL MARGINS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ATYPICAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Microcalcifications are present  The infiltrating lobular carcinoma grows as several apparently discrete nodules that measure in aggregate approximately 1 2cm  This component infiltrates insidiously throughout portions of the specimen  No definite vascular invasion is identified  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 23 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we com