Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 98 at 12 28 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3  EXTENDING TO THE SUPEROMEDIAL RESECTION MARGIN AND CLOSE TO THE SUPERIOR MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  NOTE  Definitive lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is not seen  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  DISTANT FROM THE TRUE NEW INFERIOR MARGIN  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FEW SCATTERED FOCI  FINAL MEDIAL SUPERIOR MARGIN  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE MM  DISTANT FROM THE NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Non caseating granulomas are present in two lymph nodes  PAS and AFB stains will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 12                                                                                     SPECIAL STAINS Addendum     Special stains for fungus and acid fast bacilli are negative  Added by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  14 MAY 98 at 12 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 4cm portion of oriented breast tissue  A short suture designates the superficial margin  long and short sutures the inferior margin  and two long sutures the medial margin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with surrounding hard  white tissue  highly suspicious for tumor measuring 3 7cm in greatest dimension  radiating up to 0 8cm from the edge of the biopsy cavity  and approaching the superomedial and posteromedial margins  A second suspicious area  distant from the first area  measures 1 7cm in greatest dimension and approaches the superior margin of the specimen  SECTION CODE  A  Medial most section  B D  Closest superior margin  E F  Second lesion at superior margins  G   Representative section of superficial margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Part II   Final Inferior Margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast tissue  which is inked black  The inferior and deep margins are over inked blue  which had been previously designated