n margin is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm vaguely stellate gray white fibrous area surrounded by focal bright yellow orange discoloration  The area comes to 0 4cm of the deep margin at the 11 o clock position  The surrounding fibrous tissue and the remainder of the breast tissue shows dense gray white to pink diffusely cystic fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals several tan pink possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 5cm  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue from mid inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Stellate area with closest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  pigmented lesion   is a 15 x 7 6cm triangular portion of tan pink skin  excised to a depth of 2 6cm  The skin surface shows a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm dark tan brown macule with lobulated borders  which comes to 1 3cm of the closest margin  The closest margin bears a green synthetic stitch  The lesion has been previously encircled with purple ink  On sectioning  the lesion comes to 1 7cm of the deep margin  Additional sectioning reveals unremarkable tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue with no gross abnormality  The entire lesion to closest margin is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION , Unknown.
