eceptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of several pieces of breast tissue sent with orienting mammogram inked and sectioned to reveal  fragmentation precludes assessment of true margins  to reveal a 0 2cm in diameter firm area within one fragment to small to freeze  Nodule is submitted in A and B  remaining tissue in C J  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FIRM AREA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
