lue of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 32     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm semifirm  tan yellow breast biopsy with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white  poorly circumscribed lesion  1 0cm in greatest dimension  grossly abutting an inked resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is notable for a mixture of white fibrous tissue and soft yellow adipose tissue  Representative section of lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the lesion is in A through E  remainder of specimen in F through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Positive.
