y pink area which focally abuts the black inked margin  The remaining cut surface shows diffuse dense gray white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the entire indurated area as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional tissue processed  Note  Additional sections   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   of the first excisional specimen reveal high grade ductal carcinoma in situ in 4 of 6 sections  An addition  a focus highly suspicious for microinvasion is present   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    however  in examining multiple levels of the focus  it is not unequivocal  Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL   EXCISION , Negative.
