 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast tissue  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm with a grossly unremarkable nipple  An attached axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Sectioning reveals a white  hard lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm which grossly approaches the deep margin which is the closest margin to 0 2cm  Section code  AandB  lesion and deep margin C G  representative sections of lesion H L  lymph nodes from axillary tail Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary tissue  is a single piece of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Submitted in toto in cassette M  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Positive.
