e anterior margin  slide C   1 1cm from the inferior margin  slide D   2 0cm from the lateral margin  slide E  en face   and 2 5cm from the medial margin  A second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  firm  gritty  white nodule is located 0 1cm from the anterior margin  frozen  section is taken from this nodule and saved for hormone receptor studies   0 7cm from the medial margin  slide G  en face   1 0cm from the deep margin  slide F  with yellow ink   1 5cm from the inferior margin  slide F  with blue ink   2 5cm from the superior margin  and 5 0cm from the lateral margin  Both nodules are surrounded by freely mobile unremarkable breast parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Additional breast margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with sutures marking the superior and medial aspects of the specimen  The medial aspect is inked in black  the superior aspect is inked in blue  and the remainder is inked in yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned inferior to superior and submitted entirely in cassettes H through O  respectively  Received in formalin  labeled  Left axillary tissue  A    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of three portions of fibroadipose tissue containing lymph nodes  The specimen is submitted entirely as P  Received in formalin  labeled  Left axillary contents  C    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of adipose tissue containing ten lymph nodes  ranging in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm  The lymph nodes are submitted in Q S  SECTION CODE  A  larger nodule with superior margin  B  larger nodule with deep margin  C  larger nodule with anterior margin  D  larger nodule with inferior margin  E  lateral margin  F  smaller nodule  corresponding to nodule from which frozen section was taken  with anterior  inferior  and deep margins  G  medial margin  H O  additional breast margins   anteromedial  P S  lymph nodes  Resident