Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 59 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast density on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN ON MULTIPLE SECTIONS  SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  There is no evidence of blood vascular or lymphatic invasion  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU LOW GRADE  SMALL FOCUS   0 3 CM   PRESENT ADJACENT TO BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   2 THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA 3 THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN 18 LYMPH NODES  Note  The margins of resection are free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  ill defined area that is 0 4cm from the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in A D  Labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm skin ellipse containing a 5 0cm sutured excision site and an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  The deep margin is inked  specimen is sectioned to reveal a biopsy site which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in overall dimensions and comes to 1 0cm from the deep margin  closest margin   Section code  E  biopsy cavity and closest  deep  margin F H  representative sections of the biopsy cavity I J  representative sections of fibrotic area adjacent to the biopsy cavity K  unremarkable breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity L P  lymph nodes Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby 