Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 41 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast FNA at New England Deaconess Hospital positive for adenocarcinoma  Strong family history of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast biopsy  are two pieces of fibrofatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm firm mass in the smaller specimen that abuts the inked resection margin  No frozen section is done on this lesion  The lesion is in submitted entirely in cassettes A through C  with representative sections of smaller biopsy in D and E  The larger biopsy is sectioned to reveal no grossly suspicious lesions  Representative sections of the larger biopsy are submitted in cassettes F through J  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY    report_end  , Positive.
