 x  6cm biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is irregular and focally hemorrhagic and is 0 3cm from the skin margin  0 9cm from the deep margin   the closest margin  and 4 0cm from the lateral margin  The tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is indurated with focally bright yellow changes and is focally gritty  The remaining parenchyma is composed primarily of dense fibroadipose tissue  There is a 14 x 7 x 2 5cm portion of attached axillary tail which is sectioned to reveal multiple  8  lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest skin margin  B  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest deep margin  C D  Representative sections of gritty biopsy cavity  E  Biopsy cavity in relation to adjacent fibrous tissue  F  Biopsy cavity in relation to inverted nipple  G I  Representative sections of lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional axillary contents  are two fragmented gray lymph nodes each with a small amount of attached adipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Each is bisected and entirely submitted in cassettes J and K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 19 x 15 x 3cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the anatomical lateral margin  patient is status post right axillary dissection   There is an overlying central 15 x 5cm tan skin ellipse with a central unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a curvilinear 2 5cm in length well healed scar which is 0 7cm inferomedial to the nipple  There is a second 2 5cm linear well healed  focally puckered scar  1 2cm superomedially from the areola complex and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm wrinkled  focally nodular scar 0 9cm from the long suture  lateral marg