pared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 20     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE lumpectomy specimen  inked as follows  black deep end superficial  red superior  medial green  lateral blue  inferior yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm white mass grossly abutting the superficial and deep margins  Tumor and adjacent superficial margin are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Tumor and adjacent deep margin is frozen as FX 2  FX 2 is submitted in cassette A  Section Code  B  tumor with superficial  deep and inferior yellow margin  superficial and is fatty   C  Anterior and deep tissue   superficial fatty   D  Tumor  superior  E  most lateral tissue  radial  F  Most medial tissue  radial  G  firm tissue  inferior  Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  submitted in cassettes H L  Labeled  additional left axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and tiny lymph nodes measuring less than 0 3cm each  Tissue submitted entirely in cassettes M N  Labeled  left breas